Yep, you guys are perfectly right, group access is going to give 
you write access, with the specific rules given. 

This is one notorious flaw of unix: you have to ask root whenever you need 
a new group/user, whereas it's safest to have new group/users for any 
problematic application that needs setuid/setgid.

Assuming you can't ask for a new group to which you would belong (say,
group nethack), doing things setuid, with adjusted permissions is about
the safest you can get.


